# check-reexec-coverage.baseline
#
# struct syscallentry blocks that have .sanitise = but do NOT carry the
# static REEXEC_SANITISE_OK flag, a rejection comment, or AVOID_REEXEC.
# Each entry listed here uses the per-invocation dynamic path:
#   rec->flags |= REEXEC_OK
# within its sanitise function, and documents the reason there.
#
# Format: <relative/path/from/repo/root>:<entry_name>  # <brief reason>
#
# This baseline must NEVER grow without a clear explanation.  The goal
# is to shrink it over time as arm-by-arm variation is resolved.  When
# an entry acquires REEXEC_SANITISE_OK or a rejection comment, remove
# it here (the gate will remind you if you forget -- stale entries fail
# the check).

# --- known-dynamic: per-invocation rec->flags |= REEXEC_OK ---
syscalls/fs/mount/fsconfig.c:syscall_fsconfig          # mixed arms: SET_* arms clean, others not; publishes REEXEC_OK per-invocation
syscalls/ipc/sysv/semctl.c:syscall_semctl               # semun payload arm variation; clean arms publish REEXEC_OK per-invocation
syscalls/keyctl/keyctl.c:syscall_keyctl                 # multiplexer across keyctl ops; REEXEC_OK published per clean arm
syscalls/process/prctl.c:syscall_prctl                  # multiplexer; scalar-only arms publish REEXEC_OK, others do not qualify
syscalls/quota/quotactl_fd.c:syscall_quotactl_fd        # Q_GETQUOTA/Q_GETNEXTQUOTA arms clean; SET_* arms not; per-invocation REEXEC_OK
syscalls/x86/x86_64/arch_prctl.c:syscall_arch_prctl    # getter arms call rt_sigprocmask; non-getter subset publishes REEXEC_OK
